  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data above 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 429.78 K, melting point of In; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.780$ kcal/mol. \n965 K, melting point of InS; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.600$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-965 K:</td><td> $Cp^o = 11.613 + 3.112x10^{-3}T - 0.925x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">965-1400 K:</td><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = 11.613x10^{-3}T + 1.556x10^{-6}T^2 + 0.925x10^2T^{-1} - 3.911$  $Cp^o = 14.500$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = 14.500x10^{-3}T + 3.448$ </td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-429.78 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -48.966 + 4.822 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 3.366 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 141.050 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -48.966 - 4.822 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 3.366 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 70.525 \\text{T}^{-1} + 55.192 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">429.78-965 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -48.607 + 0.474 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 1.406 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 75.350 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -48.607 - 0.474 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 1.406 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 37.675 \\text{T}^{-1} + 30.227 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">965-1400 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -41.248 + 3.361 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.150 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 17.150 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -41.248 - 3.361 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.150 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 8.575 \\text{T}^{-1} + 40.989 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Mills (80). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from Mamedov (76). High-temperature data estimated. Estimates of fusion data and heat capacity of liquid from Mills. ",
